# Reviewed required-suite exceptions for glibc 2.44 (with upstream_fixes-3) built
# in the LFS chroot. Format and review rules: README.md in this directory.
#
# Basis: The LFS 13.1-systemd glibc page states "io/tst-lchmod is known to fail
#   in the LFS chroot environment."
#   https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/lfs/view/13.1-systemd/chapter08/glibc.html
#   The retained output shows why: after its lchmod and fchmodat checks pass,
#   the test enters a private mount namespace and compares its open file
#   descriptors with a snapshot taken earlier. Inside a chroot the kernel then
#   reports the /proc/self/fd link targets as paths outside the chroot
#   ("Differences found in descriptor set": descriptors 1 and 2 changed from
#   /sources/... to the builder's path of the same files), and the test counts
#   that as a failure. The chmod behaviour under test is not what fails.
# Observed: rehearsal attempt 02 on 2026-11-05, an isolated continuation of
#   failed core run 001 with unchanged recipes for this page, four test jobs:
#   6824 PASS, 2 FAIL, 537 UNSUPPORTED, 16 XFAIL, no XPASS. The second failure
#   in that run, stdlib/test-bz22786, was a 20 s timeout while the build cgroup
#   was pinned at its memory limit; it passed in 5 s when measured with room
#   and is deliberately not listed here. It has to pass.
@min-pass 6800
FAIL: io/tst-lchmod
